The receipts do not retain per-user energy, so a replay is necessary, but not a new sweep: I’ll replay only the 240 already-selected committed configurations. I’m fixing two energy-conserving rules now: (A) activity/airtime attribution, which assigns PA and chain cost to the transmitting user and splits satellite baseband overhead across concurrently active users; and (B) equal-account fixed-cost attribution, which keeps PA direct but spreads chain and satellite fixed costs across their assigned users. Rule A is the primary summed-link convention; Rule B is the shared-infrastructure sensitivity. Both charge failed transmissions and neither is conditioned on the observed sign.
